  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="3979-faad-7ce7-6a30" name="Old Kingdom Egyptian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #104 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The army of Egypt from the early dynasties until the widespread use of chariots, copied from the Hyksos who conquered northern Egypt in about 1800 BC and were later ejected. The army is a contemporary of Sumer, but there was no interaction in a military sense at least. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Old Kingdom Egyptian]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
